  data: {
    LLM: "1. Agree the order of hand types (e.g. high card, pair, two pair, three of a kind, straight, flush, full house, four of a kind, straight flush, royal flush). 2. Each deal: dealer gives five cards face down to each player. 3. First betting round. 4. Draw: each player may discard and replace zero to three cards (or four if holding an ace). 5. Second betting round. 6. Showdown: remaining players reveal; the best hand that qualifies for this round's required type wins the pot. 7. Next deal uses the next hand type in the cycle.",
    Player: "1. Agree the order of hand types (e.g. high card, pair, two pair, three of a kind, straight, flush, full house, four of a kind, straight flush, royal flush). 2. Each deal: dealer gives five cards face down to each player. 3. First betting round. 4. Draw: each player may discard and replace zero to three cards (or four if holding an ace). 5. Second betting round. 6. Showdown: remaining players reveal; the best hand that qualifies for this round's required type wins the pot. 7. Next deal uses the next hand type in the cycle.",
    objective: "Win the pot by having the best hand that meets the current round's required hand type (e.g. this deal only a pair or better wins; next deal only two pair or better), or by forcing all others to fold.",
